<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss short-time work tumbles 41 pct in May m/m.</title>
<headline>Swiss short-time work tumbles 41 pct in May m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BERNE 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of people on short-time work in Switzerland fell 41 percent, or by 3,862, to 5,548 in May from April, the Swiss Federal Office for Trade, Industry and Labour said.</p>
<p>The number of companies affected dropped by 29.6 percent, or by 306, to 727.</p>
<p>Lost working hours fell by 43.9 percent, or 257,694, to 329,102.</p>
<p>In May, 1996, 804,720 hours had been lost among 15,193 people and 1,215 companies.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
